# Dragon Magazine Compendium - alternative class features for classes of Expanded Psionics Handbook (loaded only with it; acf_build.py).

Change Shape	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Change Shape (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Egoist	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Change Shape (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Egoist psions only. You gain the minor change shape ability that is possessed by changelings. Minor Change Shape (Su): Changelings have the supernatural ability to alter their appearance as though using a disguise self spell that affects their bodies but not their possessions. This ability is not an illusory effect, but a minor physical alteration of a changeling's facial features, skin color and texture, and size, within the limits described for the spell. A changeling can use this ability at will, and the alteration lasts until she changes shape again. A changeling reverts to her natural form when killed. A true seeing spell reveals her natural form. When using this ability to create a disguise, a changeling receives a +10 circumstance bonus on Disguise checks. Using this ability is a full-round action. Changeling Egoist A changeling's aptitude at reshaping his body makes him naturally inclined toward psionic powers that perform similar tasks, such as those of the psychometabolism discipline. The egoist - a psion who specializes in psychometabolic powers - is an avenue often pursued by psionic changelings; such characters are well-known for their superior mastery of the discipline. Hit Die: d4. Requirements To take a changeling egoist substitution level, a character must be a changeling about to take his 1st, 3rd, or 5th level of egoist. Class Skills Changeling egoist substitution levels have the class skills of the standard egoist class, plus Bluff and Disguise. Skill Points at Each Level: 4 + Int modifier (or four times this number as a beginning character). Table: Changeling Egoist Racial Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Change Shape	KEY:ACF ~ Change Shape (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Egoist psions only. You gain the minor change shape ability that is possessed by changelings. Minor Change Shape (Su): Changelings have the supernatural ability to alter their appearance as though using a disguise self spell that affects their bodies but not their possessions. This ability is not an illusory effect, but a minor physical alteration of a changeling's facial features, skin color and texture, and size, within the limits described for the spell. A changeling can use this ability at will, and the alteration lasts until she changes shape again. A changeling reverts to her natural form when killed. A true seeing spell reveals her natural form. When using this ability to create a disguise, a changeling receives a +10 circumstance bonus on Disguise checks. Using this ability is a full-round action. Changeling Egoist A changeling's aptitude at reshaping his body makes him naturally inclined toward psionic powers that perform similar tasks, such as those of the psychometabolism discipline. The egoist - a psion who specializes in psychometabolic powers - is an avenue often pursued by psionic changelings; such characters are well-known for their superior mastery of the discipline. Hit Die: d4. Requirements To take a changeling egoist substitution level, a character must be a changeling about to take his 1st, 3rd, or 5th level of egoist. Class Skills Changeling egoist substitution levels have the class skills of the standard egoist class, plus Bluff and Disguise. Skill Points at Each Level: 4 + Int modifier (or four times this number as a beginning character). Table: Changeling Egoist Racial Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Energy Snap	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Energy Snap (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Kineticist	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Energy Snap (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Kineticist psions only. By expending your psionic focus, you can create a small burst of energy. You can use it as a weapon; treat it as a psi-like ability and consider it a 1st-level power for power resistance. You have to succeed on a melee touch attack as you expend your focus and, if successful, it does 1d3 points of damage of the type of energy manifested. This ability is used more often on objects for other effects, depending on the type of energy manifested, and you must expend your psionic focus every time you use it. Fire: This can warm food, provide a distraction, and of course start a fire. Cold: This can chill food or a drink, make sure a campfire is out, and numb a bruise. Electricity: This can give someone a jolt, startle an animal, or start a fire. Sonic: This can startle someone up close or get someone's attention from far away. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Energy Snap	KEY:ACF ~ Energy Snap (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Kineticist psions only. By expending your psionic focus, you can create a small burst of energy. You can use it as a weapon; treat it as a psi-like ability and consider it a 1st-level power for power resistance. You have to succeed on a melee touch attack as you expend your focus and, if successful, it does 1d3 points of damage of the type of energy manifested. This ability is used more often on objects for other effects, depending on the type of energy manifested, and you must expend your psionic focus every time you use it. Fire: This can warm food, provide a distraction, and of course start a fire. Cold: This can chill food or a drink, make sure a campfire is out, and numb a bruise. Electricity: This can give someone a jolt, startle an animal, or start a fire. Sonic: This can startle someone up close or get someone's attention from far away. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Fate Points	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Fate Points (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Seer	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Fate Points (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Seer psions only. The Eberron Campaign Setting introduced action points with the setting. If you play outside of Eberron, action points can be used for seers and diviners as an ability to see the future and get out of its way. You can use a fate point to improve the results of an attack roll, a skill check, an ability check, a level check or a saving throw. When you spend an action point, you add the result of a roll of 1d6 to your d20 roll to help you meet or exceed the target number for the roll. You can declare the use of a fate point after you have made the roll, but before the Dungeon Master reveals whether you succeeded or failed. See the Eberron Campaign Setting and Magic of Eberron for more information and feats that work with action points. If you are playing in the Eberron setting or using action points already, you gain the Action Boost and the Action Surge feats at 1st level. These allow you to be a master of your own fate. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Fate Points	KEY:ACF ~ Fate Points (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Seer psions only. The Eberron Campaign Setting introduced action points with the setting. If you play outside of Eberron, action points can be used for seers and diviners as an ability to see the future and get out of its way. You can use a fate point to improve the results of an attack roll, a skill check, an ability check, a level check or a saving throw. When you spend an action point, you add the result of a roll of 1d6 to your d20 roll to help you meet or exceed the target number for the roll. You can declare the use of a fate point after you have made the roll, but before the Dungeon Master reveals whether you succeeded or failed. See the Eberron Campaign Setting and Magic of Eberron for more information and feats that work with action points. If you are playing in the Eberron setting or using action points already, you gain the Action Boost and the Action Surge feats at 1st level. These allow you to be a master of your own fate. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Greater Animator	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Greater Animator (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Kineticist	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Greater Animator (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Kineticist psions only. Your control object power gains the following augmentation. Augment: For each additional power point you spend, you can target an object weighing an additional 25 lbs. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Greater Animator	KEY:ACF ~ Greater Animator (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Kineticist psions only. Your control object power gains the following augmentation. Augment: For each additional power point you spend, you can target an object weighing an additional 25 lbs. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Harbinger	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Harbinger (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Telepath	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Harbinger (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Telepath psions only. You have learned to incorporate symbolism into your psionic attacks and defenses. When you manifest powers that specifically target another's mind or defend your mind, you gain an augmentation option. Augment: If you spend an additional 5 power points, you can add a mental illusionary aspect to your attack. This takes the form of a harbinger, a mental symbol that conveys a confusing or threatening message to the target's mind and momentarily distracts or disables them. The target gets a Will save to negate the effects of the harbinger. If the target fails the Will save, the power you manifest is considered 1d3 levels higher than its actual level for purposes of DC. The form of the harbinger can vary wildly. An offensive power could have a harbinger of a sword, a flame, or a spider. A defensive power could have a harbinger of a shield, a wall, or brambles with thorns. Kalashtar Telepath To a certain extent, all kalashtar are telepaths, since they share a racial talent to create a mindlink. A kalashtar who specializes in the telepathy discipline takes this natural ability to the limit, but at the expense of some of the more general features of the psion class. Hit Die: d4. Requirements To take a kalashtar telepath substitution level, a character must be a kalashtar about to take his 1st, 3rd, or 5th level of telepath. Class Skills Kalashtar telepath substitution levels have the class skills of the standard telepath class, plus Intimidate. Skill Points at Each Level: 2 + Int modifier (or four times this number as a beginning character). Class Features All the following are features of the kalashtar telepath's racial substitution levels. Mindlink (Ps): If a kalashtar telepath selects at least one kalashtar telepath substitution level, he can manifest his racial mindlink power as a wilder of a level equal to his Hit Dice (rather than 1/2 his HD). As well, each time the character selects a kalashtar telepath substitut Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Harbinger	KEY:ACF ~ Harbinger (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Telepath psions only. You have learned to incorporate symbolism into your psionic attacks and defenses. When you manifest powers that specifically target another's mind or defend your mind, you gain an augmentation option. Augment: If you spend an additional 5 power points, you can add a mental illusionary aspect to your attack. This takes the form of a harbinger, a mental symbol that conveys a confusing or threatening message to the target's mind and momentarily distracts or disables them. The target gets a Will save to negate the effects of the harbinger. If the target fails the Will save, the power you manifest is considered 1d3 levels higher than its actual level for purposes of DC. The form of the harbinger can vary wildly. An offensive power could have a harbinger of a sword, a flame, or a spider. A defensive power could have a harbinger of a shield, a wall, or brambles with thorns. Kalashtar Telepath To a certain extent, all kalashtar are telepaths, since they share a racial talent to create a mindlink. A kalashtar who specializes in the telepathy discipline takes this natural ability to the limit, but at the expense of some of the more general features of the psion class. Hit Die: d4. Requirements To take a kalashtar telepath substitution level, a character must be a kalashtar about to take his 1st, 3rd, or 5th level of telepath. Class Skills Kalashtar telepath substitution levels have the class skills of the standard telepath class, plus Intimidate. Skill Points at Each Level: 2 + Int modifier (or four times this number as a beginning character). Class Features All the following are features of the kalashtar telepath's racial substitution levels. Mindlink (Ps): If a kalashtar telepath selects at least one kalashtar telepath substitution level, he can manifest his racial mindlink power as a wilder of a level equal to his Hit Dice (rather than 1/2 his HD). As well, each time the character selects a kalashtar telepath substitut Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Personal Construct	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Personal Construct (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Shaper	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Personal Construct (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Shaper psions only. You can create a specific astral construct that you have chosen as your favored as if you had the Quickened Power feat, by only sacrificing your psionic focus. This personal construct, once chosen, always has the same abilities and appearance every time you summon it. Each time you gain a level, you may change the abilities and appearance of your favored construct. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Personal Construct	KEY:ACF ~ Personal Construct (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Shaper psions only. You can create a specific astral construct that you have chosen as your favored as if you had the Quickened Power feat, by only sacrificing your psionic focus. This personal construct, once chosen, always has the same abilities and appearance every time you summon it. Each time you gain a level, you may change the abilities and appearance of your favored construct. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Personal Space	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Personal Space (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Nomad	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Personal Space (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Nomad psions only. You gain an extradimensional storage space within your body. You can access it as a psi-like ability by expending your psionic focus. You may send an item to it or retrieve an item as you wish. The size of the storage space grows with your own power. At 1st level it is equivalent to a belt pouch, at 5th level it equals a sack, at 10th level it is the size of a backpack, at 15th level it is the size of a chest, and at 20th level it is the size of a Medium creature. You cannot store anything that has extradimensional properties, such as a bag of holding , within your personal space. Any attempt will fail. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Personal Space	KEY:ACF ~ Personal Space (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Nomad psions only. You gain an extradimensional storage space within your body. You can access it as a psi-like ability by expending your psionic focus. You may send an item to it or retrieve an item as you wish. The size of the storage space grows with your own power. At 1st level it is equivalent to a belt pouch, at 5th level it equals a sack, at 10th level it is the size of a backpack, at 15th level it is the size of a chest, and at 20th level it is the size of a Medium creature. You cannot store anything that has extradimensional properties, such as a bag of holding , within your personal space. Any attempt will fail. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Psychic Knowledge	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Psychic Knowledge (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Seer	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Psychic Knowledge (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Seer psions only. You gain the psionic equivalent of bardic knowledge. It functions just like a bard's class ability, except you use your manifester level in place of bardic level. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Psychic Knowledge	KEY:ACF ~ Psychic Knowledge (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|Bardic Knowledge	DEFINE:BardicKnowledgeLVL|0	BONUS:VAR|BardicKnowledgeLVL|PsionLVL	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Seer psions only. You gain the psionic equivalent of bardic knowledge. It functions just like a bard's class ability, except you use your manifester level in place of bardic level. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Telepathic Communication	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Telepathic Communication (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Telepath	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Telepathic Communication (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Telepath psions only. You gain the supernatural ability telepathy. You can communicate telepathically with any other creature that has a language within 5 feet per manifester level (%1 feet now). You can address multiple creatures at once telepathically, although maintaining telepathic conversation with more than one creature at a time is just as difficult as simultaneously speaking and listening to multiple people at the same time. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Telepathic Communication	KEY:ACF ~ Telepathic Communication (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Telepath psions only. You gain the supernatural ability telepathy. You can communicate telepathically with any other creature that has a language within 5 feet per manifester level (%1 feet now). You can address multiple creatures at once telepathically, although maintaining telepathic conversation with more than one creature at a time is just as difficult as simultaneously speaking and listening to multiple people at the same time. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).|5*PsionLVL
Temporal Grace	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Temporal Grace (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Nomad	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Temporal Grace (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Nomad psions only. Your power over movement allows you to resist effects that inhibit any form of movement. Anytime you fail a save against an effect that would slow, prevent, or otherwise affect your ability to move, you may expend your psionic focus to get another saving throw, adding +1 for every 5 manifester levels you possess. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Temporal Grace	KEY:ACF ~ Temporal Grace (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Nomad psions only. Your power over movement allows you to resist effects that inhibit any form of movement. Anytime you fail a save against an effect that would slow, prevent, or otherwise affect your ability to move, you may expend your psionic focus to get another saving throw, adding +1 for every 5 manifester levels you possess. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Trinkets	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Trinkets (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Shaper	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Trinkets (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Shaper psions only. By sacrificing your psionic focus, you can create a temporary item as a move action. It is like minor creation, except the object you create is smaller and you create it more quickly. You can create one unattended, nonmagical object of nonliving plant matter, up to 1 cubic inch. For instance, you could create a wooden ring, a piece of paper, a handkerchief, a thin glove, or other item. You cannot create a dried herb, a poison, or other distillate of dead plant matter that has special secondary effects. The created object has a duration of 1 minute and can be recognized as a "created" object easily. This ability is considered a psi-like ability and treated as a 1st-level power for purposes of dispelling the effects. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Trinkets	KEY:ACF ~ Trinkets (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Shaper psions only. By sacrificing your psionic focus, you can create a temporary item as a move action. It is like minor creation, except the object you create is smaller and you create it more quickly. You can create one unattended, nonmagical object of nonliving plant matter, up to 1 cubic inch. For instance, you could create a wooden ring, a piece of paper, a handkerchief, a thin glove, or other item. You cannot create a dried herb, a poison, or other distillate of dead plant matter that has special secondary effects. The created object has a duration of 1 minute and can be recognized as a "created" object easily. This ability is considered a psi-like ability and treated as a 1st-level power for purposes of dispelling the effects. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
True Healer	KEY:Psion ACF ~ True Healer (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionBonusFeat1	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	PRESUBCLASS:1,Egoist	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ True Healer (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). Egoist psions only. You gain access to the Life mantle and you may now choose from these powers when choosing new powers known. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
True Healer	KEY:ACF ~ True Healer (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psion Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.457	DESC:Egoist psions only. You gain access to the Life mantle and you may now choose from these powers when choosing new powers known. Replaces the psion bonus feat at 1st level (applied).
Psicrystal Enhancement	KEY:Psion ACF ~ Psicrystal Enhancement (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.PsionACF.PsionPsicrystalEnhancement	PRECLASS:1,Psion=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Psicrystal Enhancement (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.461	DESC:Alternative class feature (psion, 1st level). A character with a psicrystal can enhance it with a one-day ritual combining meditation and special reagents: the lesser enhancement (300 gp, 300 XP) gives the psicrystal a new power usable once per day depending on its personality; at the level noted for that personality the ritual can be repeated (900 gp, 900 XP) for a greater power, also once per day. Powers are psi-like abilities of a manifester level equal to the character's total psionic class level, usually a standard action, lasting for the encounter. Personalities: Artiste, Bully, Coward, Friendly, Hero, Liar, Meticulous, Nimble, Observant, Poised, Resolved, Sage, Single-Minded, Sneaky, Sympathetic (see the compendium for each lesser and greater power; by hand). Replaces nothing.
Psicrystal Enhancement	KEY:ACF ~ Psicrystal Enhancement (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psion Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.461	DESC:A character with a psicrystal can enhance it with a one-day ritual combining meditation and special reagents: the lesser enhancement (300 gp, 300 XP) gives the psicrystal a new power usable once per day depending on its personality; at the level noted for that personality the ritual can be repeated (900 gp, 900 XP) for a greater power, also once per day. Powers are psi-like abilities of a manifester level equal to the character's total psionic class level, usually a standard action, lasting for the encounter. Personalities: Artiste, Bully, Coward, Friendly, Hero, Liar, Meticulous, Nimble, Observant, Poised, Resolved, Sage, Single-Minded, Sneaky, Sympathetic (see the compendium for each lesser and greater power; by hand). Replaces nothing.
Mantled Warrior	KEY:Psychic Warrior ACF ~ Mantled Warrior (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.Psychic WarriorACF.PsychicWarriorMantle	PRECLASS:1,Psychic Warrior=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Mantled Warrior (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.471	DESC:Alternative class feature (psychic warrior, 2nd level). You must choose a psionic mantle (Complete Psionic) by 2nd level: in place of your 2nd-level psychic warrior bonus feat (applied) you gain your chosen mantle's granted ability, and you have access to the powers of that mantle without being required to take them (by hand). Replaces the psychic warrior bonus feat at 2nd level.
Mantled Warrior	KEY:ACF ~ Mantled Warrior (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psychic Warrior Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psychic Warrior Feat|-1	SOURCEPAGE:p.471	DESC:You must choose a psionic mantle (Complete Psionic) by 2nd level: in place of your 2nd-level psychic warrior bonus feat (applied) you gain your chosen mantle's granted ability, and you have access to the powers of that mantle without being required to take them (by hand). Replaces the psychic warrior bonus feat at 2nd level.
Soulbound Weapon	KEY:Psychic Warrior ACF ~ Soulbound Weapon (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.Psychic WarriorACF.PsychicWarriorSoulbound	PRECLASS:1,Psychic Warrior=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Soulbound Weapon (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.471	DESC:Alternative class feature (psychic warrior, 1st level). At 1st level you choose a soulbound weapon and gain Weapon Focus with it (by hand), and your first power learned must be call weaponry. At 2nd level you gain the soulbound weapon ability: call weaponry summons this specific weapon, which grows with you - enhancement +1 at 4th, +2 at 8th, +3 at 12th, +4 at 16th, +5 at 20th (+%1 now), and call weaponry gains an extra augmentation. Replaces the psychic warrior bonus feat at 2nd level (applied).
Soulbound Weapon	KEY:ACF ~ Soulbound Weapon (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Psychic Warrior Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|Psychic Warrior Feat|-1|PRECLASS:1,Psychic Warrior=2	SOURCEPAGE:p.471	DESC:At 1st level you choose a soulbound weapon and gain Weapon Focus with it (by hand), and your first power learned must be call weaponry. At 2nd level you gain the soulbound weapon ability: call weaponry summons this specific weapon, which grows with you - enhancement +1 at 4th, +2 at 8th, +3 at 12th, +4 at 16th, +5 at 20th (+%1 now), and call weaponry gains an extra augmentation. Replaces the psychic warrior bonus feat at 2nd level (applied).|min(5,floor(var("CL=Psychic Warrior")/4))
Bonus Feats	KEY:Soulknife ACF ~ Bonus Feats (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SoulknifeACF.SoulknifePsychicStrike	PRECLASS:1,Soulknife=3	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Bonus Feats (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.589	DESC:Alternative class feature (soulknife, 3rd level). You sacrifice power for skill and technique: a bonus feat at 3rd, 7th, 11th, 15th and 19th level (%1 now; applied as feat selections) - any feat designed for soulknives (such as those in Complete Psionic) or any feat your mind blade benefits from (Power Attack, Improved Critical ...), prerequisites applying. Replaces psychic strike and all its improvements (the repository grants psychic strike without an ACF guard - remove it by hand).
Bonus Feats	KEY:ACF ~ Bonus Feats (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Soulknife Class Feature	BONUS:ABILITYPOOL|FEAT|(SoulknifeLVL>=3)+(SoulknifeLVL>=7)+(SoulknifeLVL>=11)+(SoulknifeLVL>=15)+(SoulknifeLVL>=19)	SOURCEPAGE:p.589	DESC:You sacrifice power for skill and technique: a bonus feat at 3rd, 7th, 11th, 15th and 19th level (%1 now; applied as feat selections) - any feat designed for soulknives (such as those in Complete Psionic) or any feat your mind blade benefits from (Power Attack, Improved Critical ...), prerequisites applying. Replaces psychic strike and all its improvements (the repository grants psychic strike without an ACF guard - remove it by hand).|(SoulknifeLVL>=3)+(SoulknifeLVL>=7)+(SoulknifeLVL>=11)+(SoulknifeLVL>=15)+(SoulknifeLVL>=19)
Hidden Talent	KEY:Soulknife ACF ~ Hidden Talent (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.SoulknifeACF.SoulknifeWildTalent	PRECLASS:1,Soulknife=1	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Hidden Talent (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.590	DESC:Alternative class feature (soulknife, 1st level). You gain the Hidden Talent feat instead of Wild Talent at 1st level (applied): 2 power points, psionic feats for which you qualify, psionic focus, and one 1st-level power from any list. A soulknife with this ability can take Hidden Talent multiple times, each time gaining 2 more power points and another 1st-level power (force screen and inertial armor are common). Replaces wild talent (the repository grants it without an ACF guard - remove Wild Talent by hand).
Hidden Talent	KEY:ACF ~ Hidden Talent (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Soulknife Class Feature	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Hidden Talent	SOURCEPAGE:p.590	DESC:You gain the Hidden Talent feat instead of Wild Talent at 1st level (applied): 2 power points, psionic feats for which you qualify, psionic focus, and one 1st-level power from any list. A soulknife with this ability can take Hidden Talent multiple times, each time gaining 2 more power points and another 1st-level power (force screen and inertial armor are common). Replaces wild talent (the repository grants it without an ACF guard - remove Wild Talent by hand).
Educated Wilder	KEY:Wilder ACF ~ Educated Wilder (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WilderACF.WilderVolatileMind	PRECLASS:1,Wilder=5	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Educated Wilder (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.651	DESC:Alternative class feature (wilder, 5th level). You have had formal psionic training: Expanded Knowledge as a bonus feat at 5th, 9th, 13th and 17th level (applied; choose each power by hand). Your mind is not as untamed as most wilders': you lose volatile mind at all those levels (the repository grants it without an ACF guard - remove it by hand). Replaces volatile mind.
Educated Wilder	KEY:ACF ~ Educated Wilder (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wilder Class Feature	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Expanded Knowledge|PRECLASS:1,Wilder=5	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Expanded Knowledge|PRECLASS:1,Wilder=9	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Expanded Knowledge|PRECLASS:1,Wilder=13	ABILITY:FEAT|AUTOMATIC|Expanded Knowledge|PRECLASS:1,Wilder=17	SOURCEPAGE:p.651	DESC:You have had formal psionic training: Expanded Knowledge as a bonus feat at 5th, 9th, 13th and 17th level (applied; choose each power by hand). Your mind is not as untamed as most wilders': you lose volatile mind at all those levels (the repository grants it without an ACF guard - remove it by hand). Replaces volatile mind.
Mantled Wilder	KEY:Wilder ACF ~ Mantled Wilder (DMC)	CATEGORY:ACF	COST:0	TYPE:ACF.WilderACF.WilderEludeTouch	PRECLASS:1,Wilder=2	ABILITY:Special Ability|AUTOMATIC|ACF ~ Mantled Wilder (DMC)	SOURCEPAGE:p.652	DESC:Alternative class feature (wilder, 2nd level). You gain access to a single psionic mantle from Complete Psionic: its granted ability replaces elude touch at 2nd level (remove elude touch by hand; the repository grants it without an ACF guard), and you must take the mantle's powers at your first opportunity (Creation: astral construct and minor creation at 1st and 2nd level); other powers from the psion/wilder list as normal.
Mantled Wilder	KEY:ACF ~ Mantled Wilder (DMC)	CATEGORY:Special Ability	TYPE:SpecialQuality.Wilder Class Feature	SOURCEPAGE:p.652	DESC:You gain access to a single psionic mantle from Complete Psionic: its granted ability replaces elude touch at 2nd level (remove elude touch by hand; the repository grants it without an ACF guard), and you must take the mantle's powers at your first opportunity (Creation: astral construct and minor creation at 1st and 2nd level); other powers from the psion/wilder list as normal.
